WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.890
Hey youtubers it’s charlie since Hannibal
Season 2 is coming up in a couple weeks I

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.429
thought it was time to do a preview video
with all the new stuff and things we know

00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:10.429
so far.

00:00:10.429 --> 00:00:13.920
And Valentine’s Day seemed as appropriate
a time as any since it’s going to be a Friday

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.920
show this year.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.570
If you’re a fannibal finding me for the
first time be sure to subscribe to get all

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.570
my videos.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:19.570
I’ll be doing videos for each episode.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
There will be 13 just like season 1.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:21.570
So let’s start this way.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.570
I’ll talk a little about what the characters
are going to be doing and the major changes

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.249
from season 1 and then I’ll list all the
episode titles and what meals they correspond

00:00:24.249 --> 00:00:25.249
to.

00:00:25.249 --> 00:00:28.999
One of the best parts of Hannibal is that
the episode titles are all gourmet meals.

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:30.589
Grab your fork and let’s dig in.

00:00:30.589 --> 00:00:36.149
The biggest change from season 1 is obviously
the reversal of Hannibal lecter and will graham.

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:40.670
Will is institutionalized like hannibal will
be eventually and Hannibal has taken will’s

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.719
job consulting with the FBI.

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:46.260
Based on the trailer it looks like they’re
not wasting any time in someone else learning

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.760
the truth about hannibal being the real serial
killer.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.000
The image of him attacking Lawrence Fishburne
with the knife was one of the first official

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.000
images they released.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.499
One of the big issues I had with the trailer
is the idea that it could be unreliable narration.

00:00:57.499 --> 00:01:01.480
A lot of last season was spent on whether
or not Will Graham was hallucinating and there

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.280
were several times the show did scenes that
turned out to be false memories.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.870
That being said, I don’t think Bryan Fuller
would pull a huge fake out in the trailer,

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.000
so I do think that Hannibal will end up trying
to kill Jack Crawford.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.840
Unless they deviate from the original canon,
he’s still alive during Silence of the Lambs,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.980
which takes place chronologically after season
2.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:20.390
The big theme of the season is Will Graham
coming after Hannibal with a vengeance.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.270
I really love how the show finds ways to mirror
imagery from silence of the lambs.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:30.500
So it will be like Will graham is anthony
hopkins trying to help the FBI catch Hannibal,

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.830
who is kind of like the buffalo bill of this
season.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:40.380
A lot of the early episodes will deal with
Will getting Alana, Beverly, Abrams and Crawford

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.590
to believe in him again.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:45.630
I have to say though, of all the supporting
characters my favorite aside from Gillian

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.120
Anderson, who is just flat out amazing, is
Scott Thompson.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.720
Hugh Dancy said that when they’re on set,
Scott makes them laugh so hard even when they’re

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.590
filming the bloodiest of scenes.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:58.480
Everytime I see him on screen all I can think
about is Kids in the Hall.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.460
One of the best parts of Hannibal I think
is that you know how the story is going to

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:02.460
end.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.130
So Bryan Fuller and the cast delight in allowing
things to unfold in these really fascinating

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.270
ways.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.970
Style and cinematography is a huge part of
the show.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.730
Which is a good intro to the episode titles.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.090
I’m just going to do a breakdown of what
the titles are and what they mean.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.310
Everyone open your cook books to page 1.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:21.090
1 Kaiseki - Is actually a meta term.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.910
It is both a multi course japanese meal and
it refers to the types of skills necessary

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.690
to prepare high level cuisines.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.640
This is where things get really interesting.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:36.170
All of the episode titles this season are
the titles of the different courses of kaiseki.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.850
So think of season 2 as a single meal, with
13 different courses.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:48.230
Each course of the meal has a different purpose,
texture and taste.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.260
They’ve only released details on 8 of the
13 episodes.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:55.240
We don’t know anything about episodes 2
or 3, but episode 4 is titled Takiawase - this

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.240
course is vegetables served with meat.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.459
Episode 5 is called Mukozuke - this course
is a sliced dish of sashimi.

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:06.000
Bryan fuller posted a picture from the editing
bay of Hannibal swimming.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.990
Episode 6 is Futamono - it’s a soup. and
there’s another behind the scenes picture

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.780
of mads in it.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.820
Episode 7 is called Yakimono - It’s flame
broiled fish served in pottery.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:22.040
Episode 8 is called Su-zakana - it’s a course
that’s meant to be a palate cleanser, like

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.970
vegetables in vinegar.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.940
Episode 9 is Shiizakana - this course is a
really big dish served in a hot pot.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.210
It kind of implies something really big is
going to happen.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:35.580
we don’t know anything about episode 10
but episode 11 is called Kō No Mono - it’s

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.220
a dish of pickled vegetables.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.430
and we don’t know anything about the final
two episodes.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:44.459
Like I said, there are actually 14 different
courses as part of this meta japanese dinner.

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:47.270
So these are the other titles they could use
for those episodes we don’t know about yet.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:53.160
Sakizuke is the appetizer, so I don’t think
they’ll use this title.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.550
Hassun is the second course, which implies
they’ll use it for episode 2, Hiyahsi Bachi

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:02.440
is only served during the summer and it’s
just another vegetable dish.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:05.630
Naka - Choko is another palate cleanser.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:11.700
Gohan is a rice dish, Tome-wan is a miso-based
soup dish and the only other course they haven’t

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.700
used as an episode title is Mizumono, the
dessert course.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:19.239
Like I said, the only one of those titles
I don’t think they’ll use is the appetizer,

00:04:19.239 --> 00:04:20.239
Sakizuke.

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:23.900
But as the season gets started I’ll try
to discuss the relevance of each dish to the

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.249
story in each episode.

00:04:25.249 --> 00:04:34.590
One of the really cool stylistic touches they
add to the show are hannibals literal meals,

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.500
which look delicious and make you feel sick
at the same time.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.849
My next hannibal video will be my top 5 moments
from season 1, I’ll post that next friday.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.300
Be sure to subscribe to get it!.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:49.360
And have a happy valentine’s day, have fun
cooking something or someone tonight.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.669
Right now click here for my game of thrones
foreshadowing breakdown and click here for

00:04:52.669 --> 00:04:54.650
my walking dead episode 9 review.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.509
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:04:56.509 --> 00:04:57.039
High Fives!

